    ptls_asn1_read_length(bytes, bytes_max, byte_index, &length, &indefinite_length, &last_byte, decode_error, level, log_ctx);

if (last_byte <= bytes_max) {
```

If `*decode_error` was already set before calling this function (from `ptls_asn1_read_type`), and `ptls_asn1_read_length` doesn't check `*decode_error` on entry... Actually, looking at the code, `decode_error` is initialized to 0 at the start of each recursive call... no wait, it's a pointer that's passed in!

