```

If `byte_index >= bytes_max` (because of the error), `last_byte` remains `bytes_max` (set at start of read_length). So `last_byte <= bytes_max` is true. And `byte_index` could equal `bytes_max`, so `byte_index < last_byte` would be false. So the while loop wouldn't execute. OK that seems fine.

